From d76c80742a795a4d07807cadd03c06da3de1102d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hongjian Zhang <hongjian.zhang@gl-inet.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:29:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] net: mediatek: restrict native DSA tag handling

The DMA special-tag bits describe the native MTK DSA header.
Checking only netdev_uses_dsa() also enables this handling for other
DSA protocols, whose frames do not carry a native MTK tag.

Use mtk_uses_dsa() in the TX and GDMA paths to restrict special-tag
handling to the MTK protocol. Clear the GDMA special-tag bit before
selecting the current mode to avoid retaining a previous setting.

Declare the helper before its first use in the TX path. Refresh following
MediaTek patch offsets to account for the declaration.

Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/24237
Signed-off-by: Hongjian Zhang <hongjian.zhang@gl-inet.com>
